TAIL(1)

NAME
     tail - print the last lines of a file

SYNOPSIS
     tail [-n count] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
     Prints the last ten lines, or the last count lines with -n. Logs
     grow at the bottom, so the newest entries are here.

EXAMPLES
     tail /usr/adm/usage.log

SEE ALSO
     head(1), more(1)
